    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0201" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v02/pg181"/>

                <head>87. Telegram From the Central Intelligence Agency Station in Saigon to the
                    Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d87-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-02-27T07:35:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                                1962—7:35 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>262335Z. Between 2 or 3 aircraft attacked Presidential Palace at 0715 local.
                    Guards responded with anti-aircraft fire by 0730 local. Extent of damage
                    unknown.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d87-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d87-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 751K.00/2-2662. Secret; Flash;
                    Critic. Also sent to the Director of NSA. Received at 8 p.m., February 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
